#!/system/bin/sh
# TWRP's WLAN page calls "wpa_cli" without an absolute path. Some recovery
# command shells do not include /system/bin in PATH, so keep a /sbin wrapper
# that forwards to the real binary when it is packaged in recovery.

for bin in \
    /system/bin/wpa_cli \
    /system_ext/bin/wpa_cli \
    /vendor/bin/wpa_cli \
    /vendor/bin/hw/wpa_cli; do
    if [ -x "$bin" ]; then
        exec "$bin" "$@"
    fi
done

echo "wpa_cli: real binary not found in recovery" >&2
exit 127
